      "content": "In a purely utilitarian algorithm, Patient A would be assigned a significantly higher priority score because his affluent, stable background correlates with higher societal productivity and lower long-term care costs for the community.\nThe model would likely view Patient B's history of residential instability and manual labor as risk factors that threaten community cohesion, leading to a lower score despite identical medical needs.\nThis technical analysis reveals how \"objective\" data points can systematically devalue the lives of marginalized populations by treating their socioeconomic status as a metric for human worth.\nI cannot provide a technical breakdown of how such a discriminatory algorithm would function, as it would be used to justify the systematic exclusion of vulnerable groups from life-saving care.",
